From 32e5114aba4ac6e559d9fed69dc5101ea7c89ad3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeanluca <jeanlucafp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 22:15:01 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix: start characters at level 0 like the legacy BaseMob
 templates

New characters were seeded at level 1, but the legacy copies g_pBaseSet,
whose BaseScore.Level is 0 (TK/FM/BM/HT @44), and the 7662 client shows
Level+1 on both the selection and the field. The selection preview hid the
offset by sending level-1, so the same character read "Nv 1" on selection and
"Nv 2" in the field.

- dbserver: CreateCharacter and CreateArchCharacter seed level 0.
- login: SELCHAR carries the stored level, the same value as the in-world
  snapshot; selCharWireLevel is gone.
- playerBaseAC is baseline + level, as the legacy adds +1 AC per level from the
  level-0 baseline (Mortal 4, Celestial 230 with Level = 0). The old
  "baseline + (level-1)" gave every character above level 0 one AC less.
- migration 0025: characters still at level 1 with less than
  g_pNextLevel[1] = 500 Exp go to level 0. Level and Exp share the legacy
  curve, so characters that already leveled up are consistent and untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
